INSERT INTO feature VALUES('derived-rules','identity','Derived rules at a model (rule T.r : l <=> r)','univalence-theorem','partial','unique','dependent provers','`rule T.r : l <=> r;` states an equation a theory''s completed rules prove, both sides rewritten to one normal form, and is proved for every model: a path over the model''s fields, each step the law or the lemma it fires carried up its context as `Path.ap` is, each rule completion derived on the way proved first from its certificate''s two paths. A model reads it as the theory''s member `T.r` and owes nothing for it: a component a model writes under the rule''s name is refused naming the derivation (`DerivedComponent`). Sides the completion keeps apart are refused by name. A theory with an indexed sort or a nested model is not read yet.','surface-lowering surface-grammar','corpus/model/identity/derived-rule.gandr corpus/pathological/identity/derived-rule.gandr corpus/model/identity/derived-associator.gandr corpus/pathological/identity/derived-associator.gandr crates/surface-lowering/tests/modules/models.rs','corpus/ledger/features/derived-rules.gandr','#1301');
